  "original_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"primary-heading\" class=\"flex w-full flex-1 flex-col h-full max-w-[1024px]\"><h1 id=\"primary-heading\" class=\"sr-only\">Home</h1><div><div class=\"max-w-[680px] m-auto px-1 flex flex-col gap-y-6\"><h1 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\">Image Sparks</h1><div class=\"border-b border-slate-200\"></div><div id=\"pm-1\" class=\"border-0 flex flex-col gap-y-4 ProseMirror\" data-context=\"doc\" data-input-id=\"pm-doc-html-74d3235e-e67f-4a70-a65d-ed66912893a8\" data-editable=\"false\" data-progress=\"\" contenteditable=\"false\" translate=\"yes\"><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-finding-arguments-in-the-world\">🔎 Finding Arguments in the World</h2><p><b>Creating a culture of argument involves helping students notice and name the arguments already going on around them.</b></p><p>An easy place to begin is by noticing all the images that surround us every single day. By analyzing visual images, headlines, and even social media posts, students build interest and expand topic possibilities for their own arguments.</p><p><b>Consider the image below.</b> What argument is being made? How might this image spark conversations and curiosity to learn more?</p><div class=\"grid place-items-center\" contenteditable=\"false\"><div class=\"relative flex flex-row justify-between group w-full\" id=\"image-view-7aaa37cb-3004-4634-a05a-ac7e8b8f8502\" style=\"width: 306.25px;\"><a href=\"https://discovertheforest.org/\" target=\"_blank\" data-type=\"image-ref\" data-width=\"49.851190476190474\" class=\"self-center w-full\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/com.appolearning.files/production/uploads/uploaded_file/5d69d9e8-3cbc-4ae4-b538-be6402f78296/Discover-The-Forest-Ad-Campaign.jpg\" class=\"w-full\"/></a></div></div><p>​Scroll through the slideshow below and consider how these images might spark conversations and curiosity to learn more.</p><p>We invite you to guide students through the slideshow and collectively respond to the images using these prompts:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p><i>What argument is being made in each image?</i></p></li><li class=\"\"><p><i>What perspectives are represented?</i></p></li><li class=\"\"><p><i>What do you need to know in order to understand the argument?</i></p></li></ul><iframe src=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vTExzTMo0g7Jw-56Kq_KmEwKQN65rQwFM2o9TTU0dD-7hXWByVsG0oHSzWklTsCASp0IAKz5Q3sLafm/embed?start=false&amp;loop=false&amp;delayms=3000\" height=\"569\" sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms allow-same-origin allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\" title=\"Iframe for url: https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/e/2PACX-1vTExzTMo0g7Jw-56Kq_KmEwKQN65rQwFM2o9TTU0dD-7hXWByVsG0oHSzWklTsCASp0IAKz5Q3sLafm/embed?start=false&amp;loop=false&amp;delayms=3000\" style=\"width: 100%;\" contenteditable=\"false\"></iframe><p><br class=\"ProseMirror-trailingBreak\"/></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-join-the-discussion\">💬 Join the Discussion</h2><p>Spend a day noticing arguments in your daily life: headlines, billboards, ads, social media posts, etc. <b>Gather some images that your students might be interested in talking about.</b> When curating images, consider:</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6\"><li class=\"\"><p>A range of topics and perspectives</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Compelling images/headlines about relevant and current topics</p></li><li class=\"\"><p>Diversity and inclusivity</p></li></ul><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\" id=\"h_-join-the-discussion__h_-share-your-most-compelling-image-in-the-discussion\">💬 Share your most compelling image in the discussion.</h3><h3 class=\"text-2xl font-semibold\" id=\"h_-join-the-discussion__h_-include-a-reflection-on-how-and-why-you-selected-the-image\">💬 Include a reflection on how and why you selected the image.</h3><p><br class=\"ProseMirror-trailingBreak\"/></p><h2 class=\"text-4xl font-bold\" data-version=\"0\" id=\"h_-earn-recognition\">🏅Earn Recognition</h2><div data-type=\"badge-embed\" data-badge-id=\"aaaa64b3-4805-4743-81a6-e0c59e60a9c2\" data-badge-type=\"micro_credential\" contenteditable=\"false\"><a href=\"https://participate.community/badge/aaaa64b3-4805-4743-81a6-e0c59e60a9c2\" class=\"flex flex-col border border-slate-300\"><div class=\"font-bold bg-slate-300 h-6 w-full pl-4\">Micro Credential</div><div class=\"flex justify-between\"><div class=\"p-4 flex flex-col justify-between\"><p class=\"font-bold line-clamp-1\">Everyday Sparks</p><p class=\"text-slate-600 line-clamp-2\">This microcredential recognizes your engagement with the Everyday Sparks module and your thoughtful reflection on how everyday moments can inspire meaningful writing. By exploring strategies like keeping a Writer’s Notebook, brainstorming with Quicklists, and building writing stamina with Writing Sprints, you’ve demonstrated a commitment to cultivating literacy routines that empower students to see the writing potential in their daily lives.</p><p class=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">participate.community</p></div><img class=\"h-32 w-32 border-l border-slate-300 object-cover\" src=\"https://participate.community/img/k/public/7770258-Module%201%20Reflective%20Cultivating%20Literacy%20%281%29.png\"/></div></a></div><p><br class=\"ProseMirror-trailingBreak\"/></p><p><br class=\"ProseMirror-trailingBreak\"/></p><p><br class=\"ProseMirror-trailingBreak\"/></p></div><div id=\"doc-capture-source\" class=\"hidden\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><ul class=\"flex flex-col absolute border-2 rounded-md bg-white outline-0 z-20 text-slate-500\" id=\"slash-menu\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"group flex gap-2 cursor-pointer p-2 items-center text-slate-600 focus:bg-slate-100 focus:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-none hidden\" tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"slash-menu-h2\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"currentColor\" class=\"size-6 stroke-slate